# PITX2 locus annotation for duck ZJU1.0 (NC_051775.1, + strand).
#
# Source: duck GTF from the cellranger-arc reference crarc_zju1_PITX2
# (NCBI Annotation Release 104, assembly ZJU1.0 / GCF_015476345.1).
# Extracted 2026-04-23 via zgrep on
# /n/groups/tabin/chlee/singlecell/reference/crarc_zju1_PITX2/genes/genes.gtf.gz
#
# BED6 format: 0-based half-open (GTF - 1 on the start).  Strand column
# is the gene / transcript strand.
#
# Isoform name assignment (CORRECTED 2026-04-27 per d2j-validated isoform
# model in figures/_shared/pitx2_gene_model.R + pipeline/d2j_pitx2_iso-
# form_per_genotype.py):
#
#   GTF transcript        TSS         d2j ex1 window           Isoform
#   XM_038178818.1        3,961,387   3,961,387 - 3,961,458    PITX2a
#   XM_027456453.2        3,964,253   3,964,253 - 3,964,353    PITX2b
#   XM_027456452.2        3,971,385   3,971,385 - 3,972,064    PITX2c
#
# Prior labels in this file ("PITX2c_provisional" at 3,961,386,
# "PITX2_middle_provisional" at 3,964,252, "PITX2a_provisional" at
# 3,971,384) had the a/c assignment INVERTED from the corrected model
# above.  The provisional labels mirrored a chick orthology guess
# (PITX2c on a distal upstream promoter under NODAL/Foxh1) that did
# not survive d2j's per-isoform UMI-window analysis at HH13 — the
# laterality-specific PITX2c reads localised to the TSS at 3,971,385
# (the proximal-most TSS), not 3,961,387 (the distal-most TSS).
#
# Production consumers (f5_pitx2_region_counts.py, f6_chromatin_metrics
# _hh1716.py) already used the CORRECTED coordinates internally; only
# the BED label strings were stale.  Fixing them here so downstream
# readers (manuscripts, exploratory scripts, peak diagnostics) read
# consistent labels.
#
# Chick correspondence (same 3-TSS pattern, + strand, synteny block):
#   duck XM_038178818.1  TSS 3,961,387  <->  chick XM_025149516.1  TSS 57,785,032
#   duck XM_027456453.2  TSS 3,964,253  <->  chick XM_025149515.1  TSS 57,787,817
#   duck XM_027456452.2  TSS 3,971,385  <->  chick NM_205010.1     TSS 57,794,829
# figures/data/pitx2_playrr_synteny_blocks.tsv carries the parent
# synteny block (duck 2,883,389 - 4,370,912  <->  chick 56,226,160 -
# 57,705,466, 79.83% ungapped identity).  Note the chick PITX2 locus
# falls ~80 kb outside that particular synteny block entry in the TSV;
# the block is an alignment fragment, not the full orthologous window.
# The TSS correspondence above was made directly from the NCBI duck
# and chick GTFs, not from synteny projection.
#
# Primary fig03 panel C uses the "gene|PITX2" entry to pick the
# promoter peak.  Supplementary panel F uses "locus_50kb|PITX2".
# The three "tss|..." entries feed the per-isoform workflow.  The three
# "promoter|..." rows are TSS ± 300 bp (601 bp inclusive); they are the
# canonical region used by the f5/f6 region counters and mirror the
# CFC1 BED's `promoter|CFC1` row.  Loaded via
# `pipeline/_locus_bed.py::load_locus_regions`.
#
# chrom        start      end        name                                              score  strand
NC_051775.1	3961386	3961387	tss|XM_038178818.1|PITX2a	0	+
NC_051775.1	3964252	3964253	tss|XM_027456453.2|PITX2b	0	+
NC_051775.1	3971384	3971385	tss|XM_027456452.2|PITX2c	0	+
NC_051775.1	3961086	3961687	promoter|PITX2a	0	+
NC_051775.1	3963952	3964553	promoter|PITX2b	0	+
NC_051775.1	3971084	3971685	promoter|PITX2c	0	+
NC_051775.1	3961386	3976254	gene|PITX2	0	+
NC_051775.1	3911386	4026254	locus_50kb|PITX2	0	+
